# counter harness. One force call is one HarnessCounter entry.
# The potential is Lennard-Jones, epsilon 1, sigma 1, cutoff 40, no shift.
# A success is under the cap and at or below the Cambridge minimum plus 0.001.
# Basin hopping. Each quench is NLopt LD_LBFGS. A trial coordinate step is limited to 0.2 because Luksan L-BFGS has no step cap, and a long step dissociates the cluster. Displacement is 0.5 and kT is 0.8, the archived basin-hopping schedule. Pairs closer than 0.9 use a quadratic core matched to the 12-6 value and slope. The recorded energy is the harness potential. The seed is the start index.
